-#include <dt-bindings/iio/qcom,spmi-adc7-pm8350.h>
	pm8350_die_temp {
		reg = <PM8350_ADC7_DIE_TEMP>;
		label = "pm8350_die_temp";
		qcom,pre-scaling = <1 1>;
	};
```
Reason:
The inclusion of definitions for `pm8350` and `pmr735b` in the device tree for the `sc7280-idp` board leads to misconfiguration because these PMICs are not present on the board. This can cause errors during hardware initialization as the system attempts to access non-existent hardware components.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
-#include <dt-bindings/iio/qcom,spmi-adc7-pmr735b.h>
-#include <dt-bindings/iio/qcom,spmi-adc7-pm8350.h>
	pm8350_die_temp {
		reg = <PM8350_ADC7_DIE_TEMP>;
		label = "pm8350_die_temp";
		qcom,pre-scaling = <1 1>;
	};
```
Reason:
The removal of the definitions for `pm8350` and `pmr735b` from the device tree eliminates the misconfiguration issue, ensuring that the device tree accurately reflects the hardware present on the `sc7280-idp` board. This prevents errors during hardware initialization by ensuring that only valid components are referenced.

